    "reasoning": "All ten current selections agree with their own captured worked solutions and with the mathematics. q-141513: (y+6)^2=y^2+12y+36, so retain -3. q-140281: (x-5)^2=x^2-10x+25, so retain +1. q-140283: (x-11)^2=x^2-22x+121, so retain -4. q-141539: matching coefficients gives p=3 and q=14-9=5. q-141622: matching coefficients gives p=-5 and q=30-25=5. The supplied graph images now independently verify the earlier selections: q-113324 has coordinate-axis asymptotes and points (1,5), (-1,-5); q-99064 has those asymptotes and points (1,1.5), (-1,-1.5); q-97949 has those asymptotes and points (1,-0.75), (-1,0.75); q-99068 has those asymptotes and points (1,-0.25), (-1,0.25). For q-98004, the asymptotes are x=-1 and y=0, with points (0,0.5) and (-2,-0.5), as required by y=1/[2(x+1)]. Each selected graph also exactly matches the final image referenced by its own worked solution. The earlier answers remain unchanged. No captured grade was supplied; MA evidence comes from the worked solutions.",
